## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Corridor Grid Resolution for Kolkata (35m vs 10m)**:
> In Kolkata, Kestopur to Ruby spans 12.2 km $\times$ 6.7 km. Using a 35m cell size yields a $350 \times 190$ grid (66,500 cells), allowing the 2D Saint-Venant flood simulation to complete in ~1.5 seconds. At 10m, it would take ~45 seconds. 35m perfectly matches the native 30m resolution of Copernicus / SRTM satellite data.

> [!NOTE]
> No existing Mumbai code or data will be deleted or broken. Both cities will be selectable interactively in `navigate.py` or via CLI arguments, and arbitrary coordinates will be automatically detected.

