## Proposed Changes

### 1. Data Pipeline & City Assets

#### [NEW] [build_kolkata_corridor.py](file:///c:/Users/aksha/urbanFlood/backend/data/cities/kolkata/build_kolkata_corridor.py)
Constructs the full, verified Kolkata dataset under `backend/data/cities/kolkata/`:
- **Bounding Box**: Lat `[22.5000, 22.6100]`, Lon `[88.3800, 88.4450]` covering Kestopur, Salt Lake, Ultadanga, Science City, Kasba, and Ruby General Hospital.
- **Elevation Grid (`elevation_grid.npy`)**: Hydro-conditioned DEM calibrated to Kolkata's real topography (~3m–11m above MSL), enforcing natural drainage into Kestopur Canal, Beliaghata Circular Canal, and Eastern Drainage Channel.
- **Road Network (`road_graph.json` & `road_network.geojson`)**: Extracted from OSM including EM Bypass, VIP Road, Salt Lake Broadway, Prince Anwar Shah Connector, and Rashbehari Avenue.
- **Drainage Network (`drainage_nodes.geojson` & `drainage_edges.geojson`)**: Synthesized via Indian CPHEEO standards (roadside catchpits sloped to canal outfalls) using `agnostic.py`.
- **Flood Hotspots**: Accurately places known historical monsoon waterlogging points (Ultadanga underpass, Science City depression, Kasba/Ruby low-lying junctions).

